    verification oneCorpusPerProcessRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "026fc93d-f43b-4138-99f2-6760959aa19f"; :>> title = "Sprint 600 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-07"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "AVOIDABLE-ISSUE SCAN HELD. One process finding: the first cut's test failed because the counter it read was gated on KEEL_PERF - a receipt that exists only when instrumentation is on is not a receipt, and the fingerprint test already carried the same shape (`if crate::perf::enabled()` around its assertion, fingerprint.rs); no new item - the correction here is the unconditional count, and the existing item dcGateAnswersFromItsReceipt is the receipt discipline this belongs to. One measurement finding kept for rank 4: with the corpus and the commit facts cached, the per-guard git spawns (x44, 6.4-9.1 s under contention) are now most of `keel guard`'s wall time, so the receipt item's before number is this sprint's after."; }
